BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transfyr-ai-fellowship-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T121745Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Transfyr AI Fellowship 2026-2027 (Boston/Cambridge)
DESCRIPTION:A one-year\, full-time research fellowship for graduate student
 s\, recent PhDs and postdocs to lead a project on frontier machine learnin
 g problems grounded in how scientific work actually happens. THE PREMISE: 
 Transfyr argues science is missing an observability layer. Lab work is ful
 l of tacit decisions\, failed attempts\, operator judgment\, noisy instrum
 ents and context that never reaches the written protocol\, and the company
  is building what it calls the world's largest multimodal dataset of scien
 tific execution for models to reason over. Fellows get to work with that d
 ata. RESEARCH AGENDA\, eight named directions: multimodal reasoning (align
 ing video\, audio\, protocol text\, instrument traces\, timestamps\, gaze 
 and outcomes)\; conflicting evidence (uncertainty and calibration\, eviden
 ce attribution\, contradiction-aware reasoning)\; long-context scientific 
 memory (long-horizon state tracking\, retrieval over process histories\, f
 ailure and deviation memory)\; real-world evaluations (benchmark design\, 
 process-level metrics\, lab-grounded model assessment)\; tacit expertise (
 expert-novice comparison\, skill representation\, human-in-the-loop feedba
 ck)\; physical-world AI (embodied data pipelines\, transfer across setting
 s\, policy and assistance evaluation)\; biosecurity and bio-risk observabi
 lity (synthesis-to-execution verification\, emergent capability tracking\,
  autonomous vulnerability detection)\; and scientific execution ontology (
 wet-lab-grounded metadata design\, cross-domain causal attribution\, multi
 -scale variability mapping). WHAT FELLOWS DO: define a research question\,
  build prototypes\, analyse real multimodal scientific-execution data\, pr
 essure-test evaluation ideas\, and produce a publishable or demo-grade art
 ifact\, with direct mentorship from Transfyr's founders\, technical team a
 nd advisor network across AI\, biology\, robotics and scientific operation
 s. WHO CAN APPLY: current graduate students able to take leave (and to sel
 f-certify that they can commit full-time)\, recent PhDs and postdocs in ma
 chine learning\, computer science\, computational biology\, robotics\, hum
 an-computer interaction\, statistics or adjacent fields. Strong ML fundame
 ntals and evidence of research taste are the bar\; the call asks for comfo
 rt with ambiguity and curiosity about how science happens in physical envi
 ronments. International applicants are welcome and visa support is availab
 le for selected fellows. IP TERMS\, worth reading before applying: Transfy
 r owns the fellowship work product and supports publication subject to con
 fidentiality and IP review. This is a company fellowship\, not an academic
  one. APPLICATION: a one-page application sent to ai_fellowship@transfyr.a
 i saying what you want to work on and what resources you need\, with links
  that make your work easy to evaluate\; references are requested of finali
 sts. DEADLINE: applications are reviewed on a ROLLING basis\; apply by 15 
 August 2026 for full consideration\, decisions roll through late August 20
 26\, fellowship begins around September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Transfyr\nL
 ocation: Boston/Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US\, full-time in person. Remo
 te considered by exception when the project and candidate make it workable
 .\nAward: $125\,000 annual compensation plus benefits\, plus access to com
 pute\, GPUs\, data and project support. Applicants are asked to specify th
 e compute\, GPU\, data or support their project would need. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Full-time for 12 months\n\nMore: https://fellowship.trans
 fyr.ai/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fellowship.transfyr.ai/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Boston/Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US\, full-time in person. Remot
 e considered by exception when the project and candidate make it workable.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iaps-special-projects-roles-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T121745Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Deadline: IAPS: Special Projects Roles in AI Governance (2 to 5 hir
 es)
DESCRIPTION:IAPS is hiring 2 to 5 special projects roles to support or own 
 new workstreams in AI governance\, helping the world navigate towards a po
 sitive future with transformative AI. LEVELS AND SALARY: Special Projects 
 Manager\, USD 122\,000 to 165\,000\; Senior Associate\, USD 97\,000 to 126
 \,500\; Associate\, USD 86\,000 to 101\,000. LOCATION: Washington\, D.C. o
 r the Bay Area\, with London open to exceptional candidates\; IAPS can spo
 nsor US visas. PROJECT AREAS THEY ARE EXCITED ABOUT: (1) Bay Area to DC in
 terface\, closing the gap between where frontier AI is built and where it 
 is governed by surfacing what is happening in AI labs and technical circle
 s for DC policy audiences\, and vice versa\; (2) AI security fieldbuilding
 \, bridging a national security community short on people who deeply under
 stand frontier AI risk and an AI community short on people who understand 
 national security\, through workshops\, convenings and partnerships in DC 
 that put technical experts from both worlds in the same room\; (3) DC-base
 d special projects\, leveraging IAPS's research output and policy networks
  to build talent pipelines and the wider field of AI governance\, drawing 
 on a new 45-seat office in Dupont Circle and a 30-person fellowship cohort
  arriving in DC every six months\; and (4) programs targeting senior polic
 y audiences\, bringing policy entrepreneurs and technical professionals in
 to existing and developing research areas such as institutional resilience
  for advanced AI or AI and defence\, with participants working semi-indepe
 ndently to scope and explore new policy domains. DEADLINE: applications ar
 e considered on a rolling basis\, with applications sent by 8 September 20
 26 prioritised. HOW TO APPLY: apply at iaps.ai/special-projects. Questions
  to careers@iaps.ai.\n\nOrganisation: Institute for AI Policy and Strategy
  (IAPS)\nLocation: Washington\, D.C. or the Bay Area\, USA\; London consid
 ered for exceptional candidates. US visa sponsorship available.\nAward: Sp
 ecial Projects Manager USD 122\,000 to 165\,000\; Senior Associate USD 97\
 ,000 to 126\,500\; Associate USD 86\,000 to 101\,000. Between 2 and 5 role
 s are being filled.\nDuration: Full-time\n\nMore: https://www.iaps.ai/spec
 ial-projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.iaps.ai/special-projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Washington\, D.C. or the Bay Area\, USA\; London considered for ex
 ceptional candidates. US visa sponsorship available.
END:VEVENT
