SUMMARY:Deadline: Pedantic Research Grant (Pittsburgh): one to two week res
 earch stays
DESCRIPTION:The Pedantic Research Grant is a derivative program of the Peda
 ntic Arts Residency offering another way to be immersed in Pittsburgh's co
 mmunities: an independent opportunity for visual artists\, curators and wr
 iters to conduct self-motivated\, Pittsburgh-related research. The stay ru
 ns one or two weeks\, scheduled flexibly between the grantee and the Pedan
 tic Crew\, and is based on Penn Avenue in one of Pittsburgh's largest art 
 hubs. The grantee receives a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment\, an h
 onorarium of USD 500 or USD 1\,000 depending on length\, and help establis
 hing connections to individuals and organizations key to the research goal
 s. ELIGIBILITY: past Pedantic Arts Residency participants continuing to de
 velop their experiences\, or new candidates with a uniquely specific reaso
 n to be in Pittsburgh. APPLICATION: submit via the Open Call by 15 October
  for the upcoming cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Pedantic Arts\nLocation: Pittsbu
 rgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). For visual artists\,
  curators and writers with a specific reason to conduct Pittsburgh-related
  research\; also open to past Pedantic Arts Residency participants.\nAward
 : USD 500 (one week) or USD 1\,000 (two weeks) honorarium to use at the gr
 antee's discretion\, plus a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment and ass
 istance establishing connections relevant to the research goals. No applic
 ation fee mentioned.\nDuration: One or two weeks\, scheduled at the discre
 tion of the grantee and the Pedantic Crew.\n\nMore: https://pedanticarts.o
 rg/research-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://pedanticarts.org/research-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). For v
 isual artists\, curators and writers with a specific reason to conduct Pit
 tsburgh-related research\; also open to past Pedantic Arts Residency parti
 cipants.
