  since 1970\, welcoming scholars from more than 260 institutions in 44 sta
 tes and 23 countries. Residencies are available for conservators\, artists
 \, graduate students\, doctoral candidates conducting dissertation researc
 h\, postdoctoral scholars\, and senior scholars working on books\, exhibit
 ions\, or other projects in American art. STIPENDS via the Smithsonian Ins
 titution Fellowship Program: USD 10\,000 for 10-week graduate student fell
 owships\, USD 45\,000/year predoctoral\, and USD 57\,000/year postdoctoral
  and senior (prorated for shorter tenures)\, plus a research allowance of 
 up to USD 5\,000 for short research trips and a USD 100-1\,000 relocation 
 allowance. The Betsy James Wyeth Fellowship in Native American Art carries
  USD 53\,000 for 12 months at the predoctoral level or 9 months at the pos
 tdoctoral or senior level. Tenures must take place between 1 June 2027 and
  31 August 2028. Smithsonian employees and contractors are not eligible du
 ring their employment. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026 for both the SIFP and the
  Wyeth Fellowship. A separate Audrey Flack Short-Term Fellowship (USD 5\,0
 00\, one month) has a 1 February 2027 deadline. Questions: SAAMFellowships
